libavif 1.4.2: fix the static-library merge under clang-cl (Windows).

For a static build libavif installs `avif_static`, an archive merged from the
`avif` object library by cmake/Modules/merge_static_libs.cmake. That function
picks its bundling tool by compiler ID, and clang-cl reports
CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID = "Clang" (with an MSVC ABI, so CMake also sets MSVC=1).
It therefore took the GNU `ar` branch and ran `${CMAKE_AR} -M <script.ar`,
but on this toolchain CMAKE_AR is llvm-lib.exe -- a lib.exe-compatible driver
that rejects `-M`:

    Linking C static library avif.lib; Merge static libraries with ar
    ignoring unknown argument: -M
    warning: no input files, not writing output file
    CMake Error at cmake_install.cmake:36 (file):
      file INSTALL cannot find ".../avif.lib"

so no archive was produced and install failed. Pointing CMAKE_AR at llvm-ar
instead is not a fix: CMake's MSVC-style archive rule drives it with lib.exe
`/OUT:` syntax, which llvm-ar rejects in turn.

This patch (1) excludes MSVC-ABI compilers from the `ar` branch so clang-cl
falls through to the lib.exe branch, and (2) lets that branch use CMAKE_AR as
the bundler. CMAKE_AR is supplied by the Bazel cc_toolchain via
rules_foreign_cc, which keeps the fix hermetic -- the pre-existing
find_program(lib) fallback would search the host PATH and finds nothing next
to clang-cl.exe.

Non-Windows legs are unaffected: MSVC is false there, so the `ar` branch
condition is unchanged.

--- a/cmake/Modules/merge_static_libs.cmake
+++ b/cmake/Modules/merge_static_libs.cmake
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@
             COMMENT "Merge static libraries with libtool"
             COMMAND xcrun libtool -static -o $<TARGET_FILE:${target}> -no_warning_for_no_symbols ${libs}
         )
-    elseif(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "^(Clang|GNU|Intel|IntelLLVM)$")
+    elseif(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "^(Clang|GNU|Intel|IntelLLVM)$" AND NOT MSVC)
         add_custom_command(
             TARGET ${target}
             POST_BUILD
@@ -116,6 +116,8 @@
     elseif(MSVC)
         if(CMAKE_LIBTOOL)
             set(BUNDLE_TOOL ${CMAKE_LIBTOOL})
+        elseif(CMAKE_AR)
+            set(BUNDLE_TOOL ${CMAKE_AR})
         else()
             find_program(BUNDLE_TOOL lib HINTS "${CMAKE_C_COMPILER}/..")
 
